            "notes": "Round 3 we finally can shift towards an APish build - IF you want to. [So Cooked](item_0d93a9b8-c485-4ee8-accd-b706bbc23cfb) pairs with our  [Lille F\u00e6lde](item_d92c59ae-b2f5-48e5-9f60-66144441eee8) and makes our 'E' + Rightclicks that much more impactful.\n\n\nIF you want to sell any of your two survival overhealth items from the previous round, I'd suggest you keep [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0) for dash survivability & that CD reduction. Sell [Tourniquet](item_f457a404-70c1-4f1b-b6da-8fa2e90aad54) if you need to for the Epic AP item - UNLESS there is an enemy picking you off when you jump in the air...in that case you can sell  [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0).\n\nKeeping both isn't a bad option here either.\n\nFor your first Epic AP item you have a choice - \n\nMy new Favorite item is  [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) - 15% AD + Armor regen (and Armor) with your 2 overhealth abilities is CRAZY annoying for your opponents to deal with. This one is my pref, but the other two items below can work too-\n\nShooting high HP Tanks or facing Squishies that can evade/nullify your burst damage -  [Three-tap Tommygun](item_39c5d2a4-1db0-444f-86d9-2a1e9a331429).\n\nFor Killing easy squishies -  [Mark of the Kitsune](item_09a53e39-25aa-4f66-ba51-bedbc543a1eb) will blow them up. This is pretty worthless with a good kiri opposing you however.",
